## PHẦN 13: TOKEN OPTIMIZATION HINTS

### 13.1 Context Loading Strategy

> **Nguyên tắc:** Chỉ load những context cần thiết, không hơn không kém.

#### 13.1.1 Minimal Sufficient Context

```yaml
# RULE: Load context proportional to task complexity

SIMPLE TASK (fix one function):
  └── Load: only that function + tests
  └── Token estimate: ~500-1K tokens

MEDIUM TASK (add feature):
  └── Load: feature module + related modules + tests
  └── Token estimate: ~2-5K tokens

COMPLEX TASK (new system):
  └── Load: architecture docs + key modules + tests
  └── Token estimate: ~10-20K tokens

ENTERPRISE TASK (full system):
  └── Load: architecture + patterns + key implementations
  └── Token estimate: ~30-50K tokens
```

#### 13.1.2 Context Priority Order

```
CONTEXT LOADING ORDER (by priority):

1. SESSION CONTEXT
   • Recent changes in conversation
   • Current task state
   • Active decisions
   
2. PROJECT CONTEXT
   • Tech stack (from package.json, requirements.txt)
   • Key patterns (from existing code)
   • Constraints (from README, docs)
   
3. TASK CONTEXT (only when needed)
   • Specific file contents
   • Related tests
   • Documentation

4. EXTERNAL CONTEXT (last resort)
   • Web search
   • External docs
   • Stack Overflow
```

### 13.2 Token Budget Estimation

#### 13.2.1 Per-Phase Token Budget

```yaml
token_budget:
  request_analysis:
    input_tokens: "~100-500 (request text)"
    output_tokens: "~200-500 (analysis)"
    total: "~300-1K tokens"
    
  skill_detection:
    input_tokens: "~500-1K (rules reference)"
    output_tokens: "~100-200 (skill list)"
    total: "~600-1.2K tokens"
    
  implementation:
    input_tokens: "~1-10K (context + rules)"
    output_tokens: "~2-20K (code)"
    total: "~3-30K tokens"
    
  review:
    input_tokens: "~5-20K (code + rules)"
    output_tokens: "~1-5K (review)"
    total: "~6-25K tokens"
    
  TOTAL_ESTIMATE:
    simple_task: "~5-10K tokens"
    medium_task: "~20-50K tokens"
    complex_task: "~100-200K tokens"
```

#### 13.2.2 Token Saving Techniques

```yaml
# TECHNIQUE 1: Semantic Compression
# Bad: Load entire file
# Good: Load relevant sections + summary

# TECHNIQUE 2: Incremental Context
# Bad: Load all context upfront
# Good: Load minimal, add as needed

# TECHNIQUE 3: Reference vs Content
# Bad: Paste full code in prompt
# Good: Reference file path + describe change

# TECHNIQUE 4: Parallel Processing
# Bad: Sequential tool calls with context reload
# Good: Batch operations, reuse context

# TECHNIQUE 5: Cached References
# Bad: Re-describe patterns each request
# Good: "Use the auth pattern from earlier"
```

### 13.3 Context Compression Rules

```yaml
compression_rules:
  
  code_compression:
    # Keep: function signatures, key logic, test assertions
    # Remove: comments, boilerplate, imports (infer)
    
  documentation_compression:
    # Keep: key decisions, constraints, patterns
    # Remove: examples (can be regenerated), verbose explanations
    
  rule_compression:
    # Keep: gate names, key checks, pass/fail criteria
    # Remove: verbose explanations (assume understanding)
```

### 13.4 Token-Aware Task Manifest

```yaml
task_manifest_with_token_hint:
  version: "1.0.0"
  
  input:
    original_request: "string"
    request_tokens_estimate: "~N tokens"
    
  analysis:
    skills_selected:
      - skill_id: "string"
        token_budget: "~N tokens"  # How much context this skill needs
        can_stream: true/false       # Can output be streamed?
        
    rules_needed:
      - rule_id: "string"
        sections_to_load: ["§1", "§2"]  # Load only needed sections
        
    context_to_load:
      - path: "file path"
        reason: "why needed"
        lines: "1-50"  # Specific lines, not entire file
        
  tasks:
    - task_id: "string"
      token_estimate: "~N tokens"
      context_needed:
        - "file path"
        - "rule section"
      output_estimate: "~N tokens"
      
  token_summary:
    total_input_estimate: "~N tokens"
    total_output_estimate: "~N tokens"
    grand_total: "~N tokens"
    
  optimization_applied:
    - technique_used: "description"
    - tokens_saved: "~N tokens"
```

